  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans, as set out in the attached schedule which forms part of this notice. \rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than five residents at any one time without first obtaining the approval, in writing, of the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not adversely affect the adjoining premises/immediate surroundings.",
    "No cooking facilities, including hot plates, shall be installed in the bedrooms of the development hereby permitted unless details have first been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. Any cooking facilities shall thereafter only be implemented in accordance with the details that have been approved pursuant to this condition.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area",
    "Prior to occupation of the development hereby approved, five long stay cycle parking spaces to satisfy the permitted number of occupiers on site shall have been fully provided.\r \rThe dedicated cycle store providing five long stay parking spaces shall fulfil the following criteria:\r \rLocation: Near entrances or main access, \rDesign: Stands, \rSecurity: Secure, overlooked, well-lit, \rFully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof, \rAccessibility: 1.2m wide, Step-free, no obstructions.\r\rCycle parking shall be retained on site thereafter, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r \rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport",
    "Prior to occupation of the development hereby approved, waste storage and recycling facilities to satisfy the permitted number of occupiers shall have been provided on site, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and waste planning Guidance for New Developments, February 2024. \r\rIn particular waste collection vehicles must be able to get within 25m of the refuse storage point. Residents should not have to carry waste further than 30m. car Parking must no block access to the refuse storage. \r\rSuch facilities are to be retained thereafter, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the LPA.\r\rReason: In order to facilitate efficient, safe and clean removal of household refuse, the location and accessibility of refuse storage and to maintain safety on the Highway."
  ],
